A||||3||eagle01||best way to clean fuel injectors?||||5||
Z||000000||eagle01||09-24-2000||08:37 PM||||i have a fuel injector assembly out of an 86 V-6 engine that's been sitting in someone's <BR>garage for about 3 years.  what would be the best, most effective but safe way of cleaning the injectors?  is compressed air (like those for tires in a gas station) safe to use? soaking them overnight in some kind<BR>of solvent?  anyone have experience on this?<P>thanks in advance ... ed||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||09-24-2000||09:32 PM||||Probably not the answer you are looking for, but when I pull my 2.8 out for rebuild I plan to have all the injectors rebuilt and blueprinted. I was talking with a few people, asking what I should have done to injectors with 165K miles. I later found an aritcle in FOSG, detailing the process and results.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.surf.to/FIERO_OSG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.surf.to/FIERO_OSG</A> <BR>Click on "general Information"<BR>then click "Fuel Injector Info". Very informative, and is what finally sold me on the idea.<P>I don't know what to use for a quick cleaning, but would recommend using new o-rings on all injectors.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-25-2000||09:25 AM||||Depends how bad they are. You can try dumping something in the gas tank. there is a cleaner that goes in thru the shrader valve that will do the best job on the car. Otherwise if they are really bad you'll need to pull the whole mess apart.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||09-25-2000||08:43 PM||||Send them to Marren Motorsports and have them professionally cleaned and blueprinted.  <A HREF="http://www.injector.com" TARGET=_blank>www.injector.com</A>  ||||reg||1
